Tom Cat wrote:
>
> so how does i#offer work?

Fresh corpse at your altar lowers your prayer timeout, might lower
devine anger, might get an artifact gift.  At someone else's altar
might convert it to your altar or might lower your luck.

> How long can I wait before I #offer the corpse?

They stay fresh 50 turns.  For some (mummy, zombie) those 50
turns were a long time ago.

> Does it matter what I #offer?

The meaner the monster, the more your prayer timeout lowers
and the better the change of reducing devine anger.  But strangely
once both your prayer timeout is zero and your diety is not angry
at you, then how mean the monster was stops mattering.  Once
you start seeing clovers a newt is as good as a dragon.  Same
change of an artifact or clover.

But before those clovers start appearing there's a big differenc
 between a newt and a dragon.  The dragon is likely to pull your
prayer timeout all the way from max down to zero while a newt
will barely effect it.  The dragon will decrease devine anger
while the newt might be inadequate.

The point is before and after the clovers start/reconciliation your
goals are different.  Before the goal is to reconcile.  After the
goal might be luck (clovers) or artifacts or prayer.



